Abstract
With the continuous improvement of urban development level and the need to
alleviate urban traffic pressure, the subway construction is developing rapidly, and the
distribution of underground urban space is becoming more and more complex, so the
subway line needs to avoid important buildings and facilities in the design, so the
tunnel is often excavated in a curve way, which further increases the safety risk of
construction. Compared with the straight tunnel, the curved tunnel construction is
greatly affected by the over-excavation and under-excavation, and the problems such
as segment damage, large surface settlement and machine jamming are easy to occur.
Therefore, the variation law of surface settlement in the curved tunnel construction has
guiding significance for the actual project. Based on the section tunnel from Emeishan
Road Station to Fuchunjiang Road Station of Qingdao Metro Line 6, the influence of
curved tunnel construction on surface settlement is studied by using the combination of
theoretical calculation method, field measurement method and numerical simulation
method.
(1) By collecting and analyzing the monitoring data of shield tunneling
parameters between Fuchunjiang Road Station and Emeishan Road Station, it is found
that the tunneling parameters such as shield machine Jack thrust, cutterhead torque and
soil chamber pressure are obviously affected by the change of curvature radius, the
curvature radius becomes smaller, the greater the total thrust is, the greater the
cutterhead torque is, and the greater the soil chamber pressure is. When the shield
machine is used in the curved section, the appropriate shield tunneling parameters
should be selected according to the actual engineering needs.
(2) According to the mathematical relationship, the relationship between the size
of the curved tunnel, the hinge device and the curvature radius is analyzed, and the
amount of over-excavation caused by the hinge angle of the shield machine and the
different curvature radius of the curved tunnel is calculated, and the functional
relationship between the amount of over-excavation and the curvature radius is
established, and then the influence of the stratum loss rate caused by segment assembly


